                                    <button type="button" class="provider-filter-btn" data-provider-filter={provider.name} aria-pressed="false">{provider.name}</button>
                                ))}
                            </div>
                            <span id="ultimate-filter-count" class="filter-count" aria-live="polite">{ultimateBenchList.length} models</span>
                            <button id="ultimate-filter-clear" class="filter-clear" type="button" hidden>Clear filters</button>
                        </div>

                        <aside class="cost-method" hidden aria-labelledby="cost-method-title">
                            <div class="cost-method-intro">
                                <span class="cost-method-kicker">How the ranking works</span>
                                <h3 id="cost-method-title">Performance, with a measured price penalty.</h3>
                                <p>Cost efficiency starts with the same three-arena Overall score. It only reduces that score when a model’s representative token cost rises above our $1 baseline, so inexpensive models keep every point they earned.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="cost-method-steps" aria-label="Cost-efficiency calculation steps">
                                <div><span>01</span><p><strong>Blend the token price</strong><code>(0.75 × input) + (0.25 × output)</code></p></div>
                                <div><span>02</span><p><strong>Calculate the penalty</strong><code>{COST_SENSITIVITY_ALPHA} × max(0, log₁₀(blended cost ÷ ${IDEAL_BLENDED_COST}))</code></p></div>
                                <div><span>03</span><p><strong>Re-rank by the result</strong><code>clamp(overall − penalty, 0, 100)</code></p></div>
                            </div>
                            <p class="cost-method-detail"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> The 75/25 blend approximates a typical input-heavy request. A tenfold price increase above the baseline costs {COST_SENSITIVITY_ALPHA} points; prices at or below ${IDEAL_BLENDED_COST.toFixed(2)} incur no penalty.</p>
